  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Labour legislation strengthened to ensure compliance with International Labour Standards</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO has been providing technical support to the tripartite constituents in Malaysia on the labour law reform and industrial relations for almost a decade. Through the DC project and technical expertise from Specialists in Bangkok and HQ, provision of support is divided into three (3) mutually reinforcing components, namely: (i) labour law reform; (ii) empowering labour inspection; and (iii) improving the labour dispute resolution system.

The work covers all aspects of the ILO Fundamental Principles and Rights at Work, namely: freedom of association and the effective recognition of the right to collective bargaining, the elimination of all forms of forced or compulsory labour, the effective abolition of child labour, the elimination of discrimination in respect of employment and occupation, and a safe and healthy working environment. 

With close collaboration with all tripartiteconstituents the ILO has contributed to the advancement of the skills and capacity of personnel in Malaysia handling the above mentioned technical areas resulting in improved laws and legislation, regulatory and policy framework as well as practices to better protect and promote the labour rights.</narrative>
  </description>
